Z||000003||ChadMan||03-27-2000||04:51 PM||||Check this, too:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/8487/billconv.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/8487/billconv.htm</A> <P>I think FOCOA has the same kit for $2800.<P>Dropping $2500-$4000 on a Fiero convertible conversion seems really costly - until you realize the new MR2 Spyder starts at $24,000.||||reg||1
Z||000004||turbo86se||03-28-2000||12:32 AM||||There is a local man here in Myrtle Beach who owns a white 84 or 85 coupe that's converted to a convertable. It looks great with the top down, and the IRM sidescoops really set it off. I haven't riden in it yet, but my Fieroholic mechanic is doing some "extended" work to it. I guess he likes it a little too much  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I plan on getting together with him tommorrow to put on some new door bushings, so I'll check it out if he still has it. My mechanic has it real bad, he either drives the 86 coupe he installed a 3800 into, or the 86GT now converted to a Ferrari Dino. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||pherder||03-28-2000||07:50 PM||||Well, I was going to do a convertible kit on my 88 Coupe.  The kit builder couldn't come thru with the top!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  I waited a year without getting the top and was coming up on moving from TX to KS so I cancelled.<P>I still have the custom X frame that has the center part that unbolts to allow access to the fuel tank.  Some of the kits had an X frame that welded into the bottom of the Fiero and the first time the fuel pump died ...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>If anyone is interested in that, I don't need it and I would sell it.  The only problem is it is as big as the bottom of the Fiero (between the wheels front to back) so it would be costly to ship.  I have gotten roll cages and roll bars shipped to me by UPS so I know this could go UPS.<P>Paul<P><BR>||||reg||8
Z||000006||batboy||03-28-2000||11:17 PM||||I don't know if he still has it, but last winter a guy in Topeka had a half finished project convertible Fiero for sale. Do a search in the mall on my name and on convertible topic.<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 03-28-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||87ECO5||03-29-2000||05:27 PM||||I just checked out the site that <B>ChadMan</B> posted.  I see that Bill has a Stage 1 and Stage 2 conversion (Stage 1 lacks the top).<P>He states that the Stage 2 kit is $3500 plus shipping.  Anyone know what the Stage 1 kit runs?||||reg||1
Z||000008||pherder||03-29-2000||07:51 PM||||Since 87ECO5 brought it up ... Bill Welsh is the person I was dealing with for the stage 2 kit.<P>I don't think he ever got any out and this has been over 2 years ago that he advertied.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Paul<P>||||reg||8
